SUMMARY:Richmond Hill Historical Society: David Mock\, "Colonel David Bridgford"
DESCRIPTION:David Mock will share the story of Colonel David Bridgford. David is part of a local group that arranged the installation of a new monument to Colonel Bridgford in the Richmond Hill Presbyterian Cemetery. The monument was dedicated in a ceremony held on October 3\, 2026. View the entire ceremony on the War of 1812 channel on YouTube (https://www.youtube.com/watch?app=desktop&v=zDghFeUYqLA) \nBring a friend or two! Guest Fee $5.00. Yearly memberships are available at $40.00 for Family and $25.00 for Individuals. \nJoin us from 6:30 to 7:00 for light refreshments and a chance to socialize prior to the presentation\, which begins at 7:00 pm.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/richmond-hill-historical-society-david-mock-colonel-david-bridgford/
LOCATION:Richmond Hill Central Library (Room 2A)\, 1 Atkinson Street\, Richmond Hill\, Regional Municipality of York\, L4C 0H5\, Canada
GEO:43.8703952;-79.4388085
